---

<Layout title={title} description={description} path="/blog/how-to-sell-computers-for-cash/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbItems} />
  <h1>How to Sell Computers for Cash</h1>
  <p class="lede">To sell a desktop computer or server for cash, assess the hardware specifications and condition, perform certified data destruction on all storage media, and obtain quotes from authorized recyclers or ITAD providers. Non-functional systems should be recycled rather than discarded.</p>

  <CtaBar whatsappMessage="Hi, I have a question about How to Sell Computers for Cash." />

  <ul class="key-takeaways">
    <li>Document processor, RAM, storage type and capacity, graphics card, and overall condition.</li>
    <li>All drives must be sanitized before sale.</li>
    <li>Contact authorized ITAD providers or recyclers for buyback quotes.</li>
  </ul>

  <section>
    <h2>Hardware Assessment</h2>
    <p>Document processor, RAM, storage type and capacity, graphics card, and overall condition. Functional workstations and servers have resale value; older or damaged systems are better routed to material recycling.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Data Sanitization</h2>
    <p>All drives must be sanitized before sale. Use NIST 800-88-compliant methods: overwrite for reusable HDDs, crypto-erase for SSDs, or physical destruction for sensitive or non-functional drives.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Get Quotes</h2>
    <p>Contact authorized ITAD providers or recyclers for buyback quotes. Provide accurate inventory details for fair valuation. Working devices typically earn higher prices than component-only recycling.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <details>
  <summary>Do all computers have resale value?</summary>
  <p>Functional systems with marketable specifications have resale value. Obsolete or damaged systems should be recycled for material recovery.</p>
</details>
  <details>
  <summary>How is cash paid?</summary>
  <p>Authorized recyclers typically pay via bank transfer or UPI after inspection and data destruction verification.</p>
</details>
  <details>
  <summary>Are old servers accepted?</summary>
  <p>Yes, servers are accepted through ITAD programs including data destruction, asset tracking, and certificate issuance.</p>
</details>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Related Resources</h2>
    <ul class="related-links">
      <li><a href="/itad/">ITAD Services</a></li>
      <li><a href="/computer-scrap-buyers-kochi/">Computer Scrap Buyers</a></li>
      <li><a href="/blog/how-to-sell-used-laptops/">How to Sell Used Laptops</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <RelatedContent href="/blog/how-to-sell-computers-for-cash/" />
</Layout>